actual_reviewers.review_body:
With the latest changes, this PR passes in Chrome, Safari & IE 11 but they fail in Firefox & Edge 18 when run from a non-localhost domain... Apparently, Firefox & Edge don't send the `Origin` header if the domains match (interestingly, IE 11 does).

If it was just Edge I'd probably just skip this test there but with two browsers sharing the issue I think it'd be best to just skip the test on TestSwarm if the domain doesn't match but keep it running otherwise. To do that, change `QUnit.test` to:
```js
	QUnit[ ( !QUnit.isSwarm || location.hostname === "localhost" ) ? "test" : "skip" ](
		"jQuery.append with crossorigin attribute", function( assert ) {
 		assert.expect( 1 );
		/* ... */
```
Please also add a comment above these lines explaining why we have to disable it on TestSwarm.

Other than that, just a few code style suggestions.
